```

Wait, for a pair: grouped = [pair_rank, kicker1, kicker2] — sorted by (count, rank) descending, so the pair comes first, then the kickers in descending order. Good. For two pair: [high pair, low pair, kicker]. Good.

One subtle point: the tuple comparison for a flush — kickers are all 5 ranks, so no problem.

